On Monday 28 June 2004 05:35 Yashichi (devnull@127.0.0.1) wrote:

> I just got my wizard to the castle, and found the wand of wishing.
> Thankfully, the charging scrolls are already taken care of from prior
> exploration. Since I'd really love to upgrade my headgear, I'm trying
> to decide whether to go with a helm of briliance or a cornuthaum.
> Aspic is a gnome with 19 Int, 18 Wis, 11 Cha at this point. My
> instinct is to go for the HoB, but can anyone make a good argument for
> the pointy cap?

You don't need more Int; at 19 you can have any spell at 0% without any
trouble, and with the Eye you get fast Pw regeneration.

A cornuthaum doesn't only raise your Cha by one (nice, but not really
useful) but it also gives you permanent clairvoyance, which is
especially useful in Gehennom. And you can enchant it to +7: two more
points of AC.

But then I'm biased.

